## Commands
$ node bench.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18081 4B                       > bench-4B-v1.jsonl     (prompt v1, parts A+B+C)
$ node bench.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18082 9B                       > bench-9B-v1.jsonl     (prompt v1, parts A+B+C)
$ PART=BC REPS=3 node bench.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18082 9B        > bench-9B-v2.jsonl     (prompt v2)
$ PART=BC REPS=3 node bench.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18082 9B        > bench-9B-v3.jsonl     (prompt v3)
$ PART=ABC REPS=3 node bench-two.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18082 9B   > bench-9B-two.jsonl    (two parallel calls)
$ SEQ=1 PART=A node bench-two.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18082 9B      > bench-9B-two-seq.jsonl (two sequential calls)
$ PART=ABC REPS=3 node bench-two.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18081 4B   > bench-4B-two.jsonl
$ PART=BC REPS=3 node bench.mjs http://127.0.0.1:18081 4B        > bench-4B-v3.jsonl
$ python3 -I stats.py <each>.jsonl
Parts: A = 20-exchange history (40 entries, mixed zh/en) + one en line and one zh line, 3x cold (cache_prompt=false) and
2x warm (cache_prompt=true); B = FX-004 ten lines, empty history, 2 rounds (labels are mine from the 01 mood table,
not the Phase-2 fixture answers); C = FX-001->FX-002 and the FX-003-shaped zh pair, reply of turn 1 fed as history.

